        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs a predicate for the given operand. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The result is computed from the argument, before it is forwarded to the base. The tag argument is used only to deduce <computeroutput>Predicate_T</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>U</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the operand argument.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>t</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The operand.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Applies the predicate of the tag to the unwrapped operand, and passes the boolean result, with the operand prepared by <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>, to the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1unary__op_1a5403004d70e9dd8508698e33cf412e95" kindref="member">unary_op</ref></computeroutput> base class constructor. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
